## sensor-src/

18 drivers, seven more than infinity6e. See the top-level PROVENANCE -- source,
upstream hash and the reason for the per-family split are shared.

## Not here yet

This family is **incomplete**. A build gets as far as compiling these drivers
and then fails on missing payload:

    kmod-4.9.84-<drop>-<libc>-<gcc>/   prebuilt MI modules
    venc_fw/chagall.bin
    iqfile/
    sensor-iq/

and separately on `infinity6b0/` in johnchia/sigmastar-lib.

Nothing has been substituted from infinity6e to paper over this, deliberately.
The MI modules are built for one chip, and before this tree was keyed by family
the kmod directory sat outside any family -- so an Infinity6B0 build resolved
Infinity6E's modules and would have insmod'd them. Failing on an absent path is
the correct behaviour and the layout now guarantees it.

Two of the four are known to be substitutable and can be filled from a vendor
tree when one is at hand -- in ~/sigmastar/ssc336q, `venc/hal/i6b0/chagall.bin`
is byte-identical to i6e's (17741e8b), and the infinity6b0 ispalgo iqfile tree
is byte-identical to infinity6e's. Note that the i6e `chagall.bin` this
repository ships is *not* that vendor file (see infinity6e/PROVENANCE), so
filling i6b0 from the vendor tree would mean the two families carry different
bytes for a file the vendor makes identical.

`kmod` has no such shortcut: it must come from an Infinity6B0 vendor build, and
its drop must match whatever johnchia/sigmastar-lib carries for this family.
Record both in `soc/sigmastar/infinity6b0.mk` as SIGMASTAR_DROP/LIBC/GCC/KREL,
which is the single definition both packages read.

No source is available for the prebuilt artifacts and none is claimed here.
